Well, a bug is a bug. A simple approach to it would be that
once there's <buffer-limit> characters written on the square
the game would not perform the engrave action with a message
that says something along: "Your square is all over littered
with runes already, and there's no place for writing more."
To me this seems the most reasonable solution to take care
of the _bug part_ of the issue.

Practically you don't need so many characters anyway; modulo
paranoia or laziness to check the engraving and occasional
overwrite instead of constantly append. Personally, once
characters get obliterated I write from scratch instead of
adding; at least that works for me. Watching other players
on NAO there's often Elbereths appended even if the current
text contains only obliterated ineffective scribblings.

